    {
      "id": 225650,
      "name": "starkenburg_alexander",
      "username": "starkenburg_alexander",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/starkenburg_alexander/{size}/1857_2.png",
      "created_at": "2019-02-19T22:05:45.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Mint with 0/8/8/7/3 I think.<br>\n<br>\nGot a badly timed THAT card (from a Pillars of Hercules I think?), followed by an inopportune Hallway Collapse to get 5 citizens in her trash so she flipped when I didn't want her to. However, once Wraith got Infra-Red, Dawn is much less scary, and Tempest healed a few turns to keep people alive. Tachyon eventually got eaten by a Kraken, but she burned her one Lightspeed before that to kill Assault once Dawn flipped back. From there, it was a slow burn of Dawn, with Bunker Turreting to Heal/Flak and Wraith keeping problematic cards from coming out (including the other THAT card). Tempest dealt damage and otherwise controlled, and AZ did his AZ stuff, tanking due to big heals and finally dealing a 11 cold blast to finish it.<br>\n<br>\n~Komori</p>",
      "post_number": 3,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:59:21.448Z",
