    {
      "id": 225653,
      "name": "bolnerap",
      "username": "bolnerap",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bolnerap/{size}/6056_2.png",
      "created_at": "2019-02-20T23:07:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Mint with no flip and no Aurora. I made sure to keep Blood alive by top-decking him with Tempest in round 1, then never killed another Citizen except when Sweat&nbsp;got brought out by RWTD.</p>\n<p>Other than dropping Infrared Eyepiece as soon as it showed up and using it to bury Devastating Aurora in favor of a Healing Light, I focus-fired Dawn beyond that. Helpful&nbsp;in my ability to win on the round after Pillars of Hercules (and thus, losing Tachyon's turn) was, on the previous turn, pulling Omni-Cannon from the trash and having it ready for an extra last gasp. Wraith landed the finishing blow, with Tempest holding 4 damage left in reserve.</p>\n<p>Final HP 5 / 3 / 2 / 8 / 5.</p>",
      "post_number": 6,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:59:21.672Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
