      "read": false,
      "user_title": "",
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>Mint with no flip and no Aurora. I made sure to keep Blood alive by top-decking him with Tempest in round 1, then never killed another Citizen except when Sweat&nbsp;got brought out by RWTD.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Other than dropping Infrared Eyepiece as soon as it showed up and using it to bury Devastating Aurora in favor of a Healing Light, I focus-fired Dawn beyond that. Helpful&nbsp;in my ability to win on the round after Pillars of Hercules (and thus, losing Tachyon's turn) was, on the previous turn, pulling Omni-Cannon from the trash and having it ready for an extra last gasp. Wraith landed the finishing blow, with Tempest holding 4 damage left in reserve.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Final HP 5 / 3 / 2 / 8 / 5.</p>",
